# What the image installs from Debian. FR_OS itself is not a package:
# its Go and Rust binaries are built on the build host and installed by
# config/hooks/0100-install-fr_os.hook.chroot. 1.x's python3, pip,
# PyYAML, bpftool and libbpf are gone: nothing on the router runs Python,
# and fr-xdp (Rust, aya) loads and pins the XDP program itself.
nftables
kea-dhcp4-server
iproute2
openssl
tzdata
ca-certificates
openssh-server
sudo
isolinux
syslinux-common
syslinux-utils
# The persistence partition (apply.CreatePersistenceOnBootMedium):
# sfdisk and partx
fdisk
# systemd-logind needs D-Bus: without it the power button does nothing
# (found booting the ISO in QEMU -- an ACPI power-off was ignored)
dbus
# the dnsmasq binary for fr-adblock-dns.service (DNS filtering); -base
# has no dnsmasq.service of its own to fight over port 53
dnsmasq-base
# dhcpcd for IPv6 on the WAN (ROADMAP FND-1a, fr-dhcp6.service): SLAAC,
# DHCPv6 and prefix delegation, with privilege separation. -base: no
# dhcpcd.service of its own, nothing runs until ipv6.enabled.
dhcpcd-base
# `wg` for the WireGuard VPN (security-lessons G8); the kernel module
# itself ships with Debian's kernel
wireguard-tools
# ifupdown: fr-first-boot.sh writes the WAN port's DHCP client to
# /etc/network/interfaces.d and starts ifup@ for it
ifupdown
isc-dhcp-client
unattended-upgrades
# ROADMAP FND-4: firmware for Realtek NICs (rtl_nic/). Many Realtek
# revisions (RTL8125, the later RTL8168s) need it to work at all, or to
# work properly, and they are the commonest NICs in the homelab boxes
# FR_OS targets. Listed explicitly because live-build's own firmware
# collection is off (auto/config); it is from non-free-firmware, which the
# archive areas already include.
firmware-realtek
